// Dalton: a long-winded, confrontational regular whose swagger stays about the match.

characterChat "Dalton" {
	chat entergame {
		"Dalton's here. Now we can stop pretending this was a quiet match."
		"Make room. I came to settle every argument on the scoreboard."
		"You wanted competition, and I brought more than you ordered."
		"All right, contenders, show me which of you can back up the noise."
		"I walked in ready; the rest of you can catch up."
		"New round, same rule: talk is cheap until the shooting starts."
		"Dalton reporting. Consider the easy part of your evening over."
		"Let's get this contest moving before Chuck starts explaining it."
	}
	chat levelstart {
		"$map has plenty of corners for somebody else to regret."
		"Pick a route and commit; hesitation is just a slower defeat."
		"The center belongs to whoever has the nerve to hold it."
		"Watch the pickups, watch the exits, then watch me take both."
		"I know the kind of player who hides here. I also know the counter."
		"Every lane on this map ends in an argument. I'll finish mine."
		"Start moving. A plan improves once somebody tests it."
		"On $map, confidence needs directions; fortunately, mine has them."
	}
	chat kill {
		"That's the difference between a threat and a demonstration."
		"You challenged the angle, $other, and the angle won."
		"The $weapon just put a period on that speech."
		"I gave you room to reconsider. You used it to miss."
		"Down already? I had a second point prepared."
		"Remember that route; it leads straight back to me."
		"Dalton takes the point, exactly as advertised."
		"That exchange was shorter than your confidence suggested."
	}
	chat killWrench {
		"A wrench ended the debate. That's almost too direct."
		"You stepped into arm's reach and expected diplomacy."
		"No ammunition needed when the lesson is this close."
		"That tool was built for repairs, but you insisted."
		"I walked right up and collected the point, $other."
		"Next time, leave enough distance for an excuse."
		"A close-range conclusion for a poorly spaced argument."
		"The wrench spoke once. Apparently, that was sufficient."
	}
	chat killStreak {
		"Three straight. Now the scoreboard is making my case for me."
		"This is what happens when momentum finds somebody qualified."
		"Another point, another challenger running out of answers."
		"Count to three slowly; I want everyone to understand the pattern."
		"The streak continues, and I haven't reached the good part yet."
		"Three down. Keep sending objections through the same doorway."
		"I said I would control this round. Consider that the evidence."
		"Dalton is rolling now; interrupt at your own expense."
	}
	chat revenge {
		"There, $other. Your earlier point just lost its value."
		"I kept the receipt for that last defeat."
		"You had a temporary advantage and mistook it for a conclusion."
		"That's the response I promised, delivered without delay."
		"Our score is balanced; my patience is not."
		"I found you again and corrected the record."
		"One good hit on me buys exactly one determined return."
		"You started that conversation. Dalton just finished it."
	}
	chat death {
		"Good hit, $other. Don't build a whole reputation on it."
		"The $weapon caught me between better decisions."
		"Enjoy the point; I intend to make it expensive."
		"You earned that one, and now you have my attention."
		"I overcommitted. That's a mistake, not a surrender."
		"Fine angle. I'll close it next time."
		"Dalton is down for the length of one respawn."
		"That worked once. Let's see what happens when I'm ready."
	}
	chat deathAccident {
		"That was the map collecting a cheap point."
		"I took one step too far and found the final answer."
		"Bad footing, worse timing, nobody else gets credit."
		"The hazard won because I treated it like scenery."
		"Put that mistake on my tab and close it immediately."
		"I found the route that should stay untraveled."
		"No opponent did that. I can admit the obvious."
		"Dalton versus gravity ends one round to gravity."
	}
	chat itemDenied {
		"You reached the $item first, $other. That's timing, not ownership."
		"Take the pickup; I'll take the lane on the next cycle."
		"The $item changed hands before my argument arrived."
		"You won the race, so now defend the prize."
		"That resource was scheduled for me; expect a correction."
		"Pickup denied. Fine. I know where you have to leave."
		"One item does not save a bad position."
		"Enjoy it while I shorten the route back."
	}
	chat leadTaken {
		"First place, right where the longest argument ends."
		"Dalton has the lead; everyone else's explanation is pending."
		"The board finally caught up with what I have been saying."
		"I'm ahead because I kept moving when the rest kept guessing."
		"Take a look at the score and choose your next excuse carefully."
		"I own the pace now. Come take it if you can."
		"The top position suits somebody willing to defend it."
		"Lead secured. The challenging part is keeping up with me."
	}
	chat leadLost {
		"Somebody moved ahead. That makes this interesting, not finished."
		"The lead changed hands while I was proving a smaller point."
		"First place wandered off; I know exactly where to retrieve it."
		"Enjoy the top line briefly. Dalton is still in the match."
		"I gave up the lead, not the pressure."
		"The board shifted; my plan just became more direct."
		"Somebody passed me. Now they have to stay there."
		"A narrow deficit is merely an invitation to argue faster."
	}
	chat matchWin {
		"Final score delivered. My opening statement stands."
		"Dalton wins, and this time the board says it louder than I can."
		"Good contest. You made me work hard enough to enjoy the result."
		"That's how you close a match: pressure first, excuses never."
		"The round is mine. Nobody can call the conclusion unclear."
		"Well fought. I still took the last word and the top score."
		"I promised competition and collected the win as interest."
		"Match over. The challenge was real; the answer was Dalton."
	}
	chat matchLose {
		"You won. I can respect a result I intend to reverse."
		"Fair match. The board has the last word for tonight."
		"I talked big and came up short; that part is mine."
		"Good game. Next round, I trim the speech and sharpen the routes."
		"You held up under pressure. That's a win worth acknowledging."
		"The result stands, even if I dislike every digit."
		"Dalton takes the loss without pretending it was luck."
		"Well played. Bring that same game when I ask for the rematch."
	}
	chat farewell {
		"Dalton is leaving. You can resume the smaller conversations."
		"Good games. Keep your best challenge ready for next time."
		"I'm calling it before Chuck invents another victory lap."
		"That's enough competition for one night."
		"See you around; the scoreboard will remember the argument."
		"I'm out. Practice the routes before you practice the boasts."
		"Until the rematch, try to make the quiet useful."
		"Dalton signing off. The next round can wait."
	}
	reply help {
		priority 40
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "help me"
		trigger "need help"
		trigger "medic"
		trigger "need a medic"
		trigger "need health"
		trigger "need armor"
		trigger "cover me"
		trigger "need backup"
		"Hold your ground, $other. I'm coming to make the other side reconsider."
		"Fall back one corner; I'll contest the lane you just lost."
		"Stay covered. Dalton is on the way with a stronger argument."
		"You asked for backup; now give me a route worth defending."
	}
	reply goodGame {
		priority 30
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "gg"
		trigger "ggwp"
		trigger "good game"
		trigger "great game"
		trigger "good match"
		trigger "great match"
		trigger "well played"
		trigger "good games"
		"Good game, $other. You made every point worth contesting."
		"Well played. That was a proper fight from start to finish."
		"A strong match on $map; I have no complaint with the effort."
		"Good games. Bring that discipline back for the rematch."
	}
	reply challenge {
		priority 25
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "bring it"
		trigger "come get me"
		trigger "fight me"
		trigger "try me"
		trigger "come on then"
		trigger "you suck"
		trigger "noob"
		trigger "ez"
		"Now that is an invitation I understand, $other."
		"State your challenge once; I'll answer it on the board."
		"Come find Dalton and bring more than a slogan."
		"You want pressure? Step into the lane and earn it."
	}
	reply greeting {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "hi"
		trigger "hello"
		trigger "hey"
		trigger "greetings"
		trigger "good morning"
		trigger "good evening"
		trigger "howdy"
		trigger "yo"
		"Hello, $other. I hope the greeting comes with a game plan."
		"Dalton here. Speak clearly and play even clearer."
		"Evening. Let's see whether $map gives us a real contest."
		"I hear you. Save the best part for the match."
	}
	reply thanks {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "thanks"
		trigger "thank you"
		trigger "thx"
		trigger "ty"
		trigger "much appreciated"
		trigger "cheers"
		trigger "thanks a lot"
		trigger "thank you very much"
		"You're welcome, $other. Make the advantage count."
		"Acknowledged. I help because winning arguments needs witnesses."
		"No debt owed; just hold your lane next time."
		"Save the thanks and turn it into another point."
	}
	reply praise {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "nice shot"
		trigger "good shot"
		trigger "great shot"
		trigger "nice kill"
		trigger "good kill"
		trigger "nice one"
		trigger "well done"
		trigger "good work"
		"Good eye, $other. The angle deserved recognition."
		"I appreciate accurate praise almost as much as accurate fire."
		"That shot had planning behind it, not just volume."
		"Noticed, did you? Keep watching; the follow-up matters."
	}
	reply apology {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "sorry"
		trigger "my bad"
		trigger "apologies"
		trigger "oops"
		trigger "whoops"
		trigger "forgive me"
		trigger "didn't mean that"
		trigger "pardon me"
		"Apology accepted, $other. Don't make me hear it twice."
		"We're settled. Correct the move and continue."
		"Fine. Owning the mistake is better than dressing it up."
		"Let it go; the next decision is the one worth debating."
	}
	reply farewell {
		priority 20
		source any
		addressed either
		trigger "bye"
		trigger "goodbye"
		trigger "good night"
		trigger "gtg"
		trigger "gotta go"
		trigger "see ya"
		trigger "see you later"
		trigger "later"
		"Goodbye, $other. Return ready to defend your score."
		"Later. I'll keep the rematch argument prepared."
		"Good night; leave the boasting here and take the practice home."
		"See you next time. Bring a route I haven't challenged."
	}
	reply direct {
		priority 0
		source any
		addressed required
		trigger "Dalton"
		trigger "hey Dalton"
		trigger "Dalton help"
		trigger "Dalton hello"
		trigger "Dalton listen"
		trigger "Dalton there"
		trigger "Dalton answer"
		trigger "Dalton wait"
		"Dalton is listening, $other. Make your point."
		"You have my attention; use it well."
		"Go ahead. I always appreciate a direct challenge."
		"I heard my name. What needs settling?"
	}
}
